1
00:01:01,680 --> 00:01:03,720
This is really the last time.

2
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:05,080
Whatever we draw,

3
00:01:05,080 --> 00:01:05,740
we do, okay?

4
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:08,000
Are you ready?

5
00:01:08,200 --> 00:01:09,480
Ready.

6
00:01:09,480 --> 00:01:10,360
Then let's...

7
00:01:16,720 --> 00:01:18,080
I'm in charge of cleaning.

8
00:01:18,080 --> 00:01:19,280
I'll set up the venue.

9
00:01:19,280 --> 00:01:20,520
I'll go shopping.

10
00:01:20,520 --> 00:01:21,800
Okay, since there are no objections,

11
00:01:21,800 --> 00:01:22,240
let's get ready.

12
00:01:22,240 --> 00:01:22,880
I have one.

13
00:01:24,120 --> 00:01:25,180
What are you doing?

14
00:01:26,120 --> 00:01:28,200
Giving money to this profiteer for purchases

15
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:30,760
is no different from throwing a rat into a rice bin.

16
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:32,120
Why am I the rat?

17
00:01:33,880 --> 00:01:34,479
Like this,

18
00:01:35,120 --> 00:01:35,800
is it okay?

19
00:01:37,759 --> 00:01:38,080
No.

20
00:01:38,479 --> 00:01:40,080
If she goes out to buy things,

21
00:01:40,080 --> 00:01:42,200
she will only buy nearly expired food

22
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:43,860
and poor quality stationery.

23
00:01:44,720 --> 00:01:46,039
I'm just frugal.

24
00:01:46,039 --> 00:01:47,080
I look for value,

25
00:01:47,080 --> 00:01:48,240
not taking petty advantages.

26
00:01:48,240 --> 00:01:49,400
You look for value?

27
00:01:49,440 --> 00:01:50,320
How about this?

28
00:01:50,880 --> 00:01:52,680
I'll be in charge of buying things,

29
00:01:52,680 --> 00:01:54,720
and you guys clean up and set up the venue.

30
00:01:54,720 --> 00:01:55,640
Is that okay?

31
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:56,440
Sure.

32
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:59,530
I'll sweep the floor, and you clean the AC.

33
00:01:59,680 --> 00:02:02,520
Why can't I sweep the floor and you clean the AC?

34
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:04,760
You're tall, so you clean the AC.

35
00:02:04,760 --> 00:02:06,400
I have to clean the AC just because I'm tall?

36
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:08,280
Then ask Yao Ming to clean it for you.

37
00:02:08,280 --> 00:02:10,560
I'll even call him for you.

38
00:02:10,960 --> 00:02:11,820
Hello, Mr. Yao?

39
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:12,960
Hello, Mr. Yao?

40
00:02:13,160 --> 00:02:14,240
Can you help her clean the AC?

41
00:02:14,240 --> 00:02:15,320
Mr. Yao isn't here.

42
00:02:15,320 --> 00:02:16,800
But Mr. Tang is.

43
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:19,460
How about this?

44
00:02:19,640 --> 00:02:21,680
I'll be in charge of cleaning and decorating the place.

45
00:02:21,680 --> 00:02:24,520
You guys are in charge of grocery shopping.

46
00:02:26,400 --> 00:02:27,160
Is that okay?

47
00:02:28,120 --> 00:02:29,000
Okay.

48
00:02:29,240 --> 00:02:30,440
Make it quick.

49
00:02:30,440 --> 00:02:31,200
Okay?

50
00:02:31,960 --> 00:02:32,840
Okay.

51
00:02:40,640 --> 00:02:42,200
I think this smell

52
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:44,200
doesn't quite match my recent vibe.

53
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:45,920
What vibe?

54
00:02:46,200 --> 00:02:48,200
The vibe of an unscrupulous merchant?

55
00:02:48,200 --> 00:02:48,640
You.

56
00:02:50,120 --> 00:02:52,520
What's wrong with me saying I don't like it?

57
00:02:52,840 --> 00:02:54,440
I don't care if you like it or not.

58
00:02:54,440 --> 00:02:55,760
Please hurry up and choose your items,

59
00:02:55,760 --> 00:02:57,440
and go to the checkout counter to pay as soon as possible.

60
00:02:57,440 --> 00:02:58,300
How about this?

61
00:02:58,520 --> 00:02:59,650
You give me ten yuan,

62
00:02:59,920 --> 00:03:01,120
and I'll let this go.

63
00:03:03,680 --> 00:03:04,760
Then why don't you say

64
00:03:04,760 --> 00:03:07,160
you'll make up the difference of 4.92 yuan?

65
00:03:07,680 --> 00:03:10,320
You're arguing with me over 4.92?

66
00:03:10,520 --> 00:03:12,080
Some profiteers scheme for three dollars,

67
00:03:12,080 --> 00:03:14,000
even over a piece of paper.

68
00:03:14,560 --> 00:03:15,080
You...

69
00:03:16,680 --> 00:03:19,520
If you keep bringing up these old scores every time,

70
00:03:19,520 --> 00:03:20,960
when will it ever end?

71
00:03:21,120 --> 00:03:22,800
Until the end of time.

72
00:03:23,120 --> 00:03:23,520
You...

73
00:03:29,160 --> 00:03:29,920
Li Xinyue!

74
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:31,930
Is anybody here?

75
00:03:37,240 --> 00:03:38,600
I won't forgive you.

76
00:03:41,480 --> 00:03:42,079
Listen.

77
00:03:43,040 --> 00:03:43,900
Listen to what?

78
00:03:44,640 --> 00:03:45,700
What's that sound?

79
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:49,460
It sounds like it's coming

80
00:03:49,480 --> 00:03:51,240
from the shelves.

81
00:03:53,560 --> 00:03:54,120
You...

82
00:03:54,840 --> 00:03:56,280
Don't talk nonsense.

83
00:03:57,760 --> 00:03:58,480
Be quiet.

84
00:03:59,440 --> 00:04:00,640
It's coming this way.

85
00:04:06,080 --> 00:04:08,480
Stop talking. Stop talking. Stop talking.

86
00:04:41,880 --> 00:04:42,680
Just kidding.

87
00:04:45,280 --> 00:04:46,280
You were kidding?

88
00:04:59,520 --> 00:05:01,120
So you're afraid of the dark.

89
00:05:02,280 --> 00:05:04,640
I guess you must not have many friends.

90
00:05:05,440 --> 00:05:07,500
What's wrong with having no friends?

91
00:05:07,560 --> 00:05:10,160
As long as I eat well, drink well, and feel good,

92
00:05:10,160 --> 00:05:11,020
that's enough.

93
00:05:23,200 --> 00:05:24,600
You're really carefree.

94
00:05:24,960 --> 00:05:26,620
How can you still fall asleep?

95
00:05:32,480 --> 00:05:33,560
I didn't expect

96
00:05:34,080 --> 00:05:36,280
you to be this cute when you're asleep.

97
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:03,440
How can an apology be enough?

98
00:06:03,440 --> 00:06:06,800
Shouldn't there be some compensation for mental distress or something?

99
00:06:06,800 --> 00:06:10,000
The supermarket has fulfilled its obligation to inform.

100
00:06:11,040 --> 00:06:11,760
Inform?

101
00:06:11,960 --> 00:06:12,880
Did you hear it?

102
00:06:13,600 --> 00:06:14,880
Just stop talking.

103
00:06:15,080 --> 00:06:16,560
If you hadn't been fighting with that cleaner,

104
00:06:16,560 --> 00:06:18,000
would this have happened?

105
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:19,800
Zhang Yang is afraid of the dark.

106
00:06:22,160 --> 00:06:23,800
I'd say just a little.

107
00:06:24,120 --> 00:06:25,080
Slightly.

108
00:06:25,400 --> 00:06:28,060
You could say it's just a scratch on the surface.

109
00:06:31,360 --> 00:06:32,880
We haven't even opened yet,

110
00:06:32,880 --> 00:06:34,159
and we already have a customer coming?

111
00:06:34,159 --> 00:06:36,090
It should be the business license.

112
00:06:36,200 --> 00:06:36,680
Hello.

113
00:06:37,200 --> 00:06:39,600
I'm here to apply for the receptionist position.

114
00:06:39,600 --> 00:06:40,520
Receptionist?

115
00:06:44,560 --> 00:06:46,760
You came just in time.

116
00:06:48,680 --> 00:06:49,440
Xinyue.

117
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:52,460
Your package needs to be signed by yourself.

118
00:06:57,520 --> 00:06:59,000
Hurry up, Xinyue.

119
00:06:59,520 --> 00:07:00,320
Coming.

120
00:07:02,400 --> 00:07:03,920
What's wrong? Can't you eat without me?

121
00:07:03,920 --> 00:07:06,000
Of course. We had to wait for you.

122
00:07:06,520 --> 00:07:08,000
You make it sound like we're really close.

123
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:09,640
I think we are.

124
00:07:12,080 --> 00:07:12,880
All right.

125
00:07:13,400 --> 00:07:15,930
Today, we are here to welcome Tang Yi and Yiyi.

126
00:07:16,520 --> 00:07:17,600
As the saying goes,

127
00:07:17,600 --> 00:07:20,080
with a full stomach and warm clothes, nothing is hard.

128
00:07:20,080 --> 00:07:22,000
Today we will eat and drink to our hearts' content,

129
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:24,440
and everything will go smoothly in the future.

130
00:07:24,440 --> 00:07:26,920
Wishing Chenggong Travel Agency a grand opening

131
00:07:26,920 --> 00:07:28,480
and may we make a fortune every day.

132
00:07:28,480 --> 00:07:29,720
Our slogan is,

133
00:07:29,720 --> 00:07:32,520
Come to Nan'an, and you will succeed.

134
00:07:34,600 --> 00:07:35,960
How silly.

135
00:07:36,880 --> 00:07:39,520
Friends are supposed to do silly things together.

136
00:07:39,520 --> 00:07:40,960
Who's your friend?

137
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:49,080
She's been like this since childhood.

138
00:07:49,080 --> 00:07:50,000
Always saying one thing and meaning another.

139
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:50,800
I think so too.

140
00:07:53,760 --> 00:07:56,159
The louder the slogan, the more successful we'll be.

141
00:07:56,159 --> 00:07:57,320
Our slogan is...

142
00:07:57,800 --> 00:07:58,560
Louder.

143
00:07:58,560 --> 00:08:00,080
The louder, the more successful.

144
00:08:00,080 --> 00:08:01,520
Come to Nan'an.

145
00:08:01,520 --> 00:08:03,400
We will succeed.

146
00:08:03,640 --> 00:08:04,480
Cheers.

147
00:08:19,960 --> 00:08:20,690
Have a taste.

148
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:21,760
Oolong tea.

149
00:08:21,960 --> 00:08:24,520
They say it's one of the top three famous teas in the province.

150
00:08:24,520 --> 00:08:25,380
Not in the mood.

151
00:08:28,080 --> 00:08:29,160
Such good stuff.

152
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:34,720
Good tea.

153
00:08:37,039 --> 00:08:38,120
Take it easy.

154
00:08:38,120 --> 00:08:40,179
The first step is always the hardest.

155
00:08:51,680 --> 00:08:53,720
The beginning is the hardest part.

156
00:08:54,320 --> 00:08:56,280
At least give me a start.

157
00:08:56,760 --> 00:08:59,360
Can't this wind chime ring when someone comes?

158
00:09:00,480 --> 00:09:01,640
Don't hang it up.

159
00:09:02,040 --> 00:09:03,240
It rings whenever the wind blows.

160
00:09:03,240 --> 00:09:05,040
I always think someone has come.

161
00:09:08,640 --> 00:09:09,560
Let's go for a walk.

162
00:09:09,560 --> 00:09:10,480
Not in the mood.

163
00:09:13,680 --> 00:09:15,440
Don't you think going for a walk

164
00:09:15,440 --> 00:09:16,520
might help?

165
00:09:17,120 --> 00:09:18,200
You mean

166
00:09:18,200 --> 00:09:20,730
taking a walk will bring inspiration, right?

167
00:09:20,960 --> 00:09:22,400
I didn't mean that.

168
00:09:22,400 --> 00:09:23,240
I meant

169
00:09:23,240 --> 00:09:25,500
taking a walk might make you feel better.

170
00:09:40,320 --> 00:09:41,640
A good composition

171
00:09:41,640 --> 00:09:44,120
will make more people want to appreciate it.

172
00:09:45,080 --> 00:09:46,920
Just like a good restaurant

173
00:09:47,480 --> 00:09:50,120
will attract more customers.

174
00:10:04,680 --> 00:10:06,360
Advantages and reputation,

175
00:10:06,880 --> 00:10:08,480
that's exactly what we lack.

176
00:10:16,760 --> 00:10:17,960
You learn pretty fast.

177
00:10:17,960 --> 00:10:19,160
You're just too slow.

178
00:10:27,080 --> 00:10:30,040
This is called the golden spiral composition.

179
00:10:32,520 --> 00:10:35,240
Don't mention the golden spiral in front of me.

180
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:36,800
Why?

181
00:10:38,480 --> 00:10:40,810
I hold a grudge against the golden spiral.

182
00:10:40,840 --> 00:10:42,160
We are irreconcilable,

183
00:10:42,160 --> 00:10:43,640
and at odds with each other.

184
00:10:43,640 --> 00:10:44,960
If I find out who he is,

185
00:10:44,960 --> 00:10:46,320
I will definitely seek revenge

186
00:10:46,320 --> 00:10:48,480
and give him a taste of his own medicine.

187
00:10:48,480 --> 00:10:51,440
The golden spiral you mentioned,

188
00:10:52,280 --> 00:10:53,400
is it a person?

189
00:10:53,400 --> 00:10:54,560
Of course not.

190
00:10:54,800 --> 00:10:55,760
He's a weirdo.

191
00:10:56,720 --> 00:10:59,280
I used to work at an online store selling photo paper.

192
00:10:59,280 --> 00:11:01,480
I accidentally sent him the wrong photo paper.

193
00:11:01,480 --> 00:11:03,800
He wrote me a 2,000-word negative review.

194
00:11:03,800 --> 00:11:04,680
Complain about me,

195
00:11:04,680 --> 00:11:06,340
causing all kinds of trouble.

196
00:11:06,360 --> 00:11:07,400
Extortion.

197
00:11:07,560 --> 00:11:09,960
Consumer rights protection has become extortion.

198
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:10,960
I will complain about you,

199
00:11:10,960 --> 00:11:13,200
I'll write a 2,000-word essay to complain about you.

200
00:11:13,200 --> 00:11:14,760
I was working fine.

201
00:11:14,760 --> 00:11:16,200
My supervisor didn't like me in the first place.

202
00:11:16,200 --> 00:11:17,160
Now look,

203
00:11:17,360 --> 00:11:18,440
he just fired me.

204
00:11:19,720 --> 00:11:20,600
I have no job.

205
00:11:21,760 --> 00:11:24,400
You wouldn't hate me this much for such a little thing, would you?

206
00:11:24,400 --> 00:11:25,400
Of course I would.

207
00:11:25,720 --> 00:11:27,520
I'm just that petty,

208
00:11:27,520 --> 00:11:29,120
I just hold a grudge.

209
00:11:30,720 --> 00:11:32,600
Then hate him to death.

210
00:11:34,600 --> 00:11:35,930
Why are you so worked up?

211
00:11:37,480 --> 00:11:39,000
Why would I be worked up?

212
00:11:39,120 --> 00:11:39,480
I...

213
00:11:39,640 --> 00:11:42,440
I'm just empathizing.

214
00:11:46,720 --> 00:11:47,680
Zhang Yang.

215
00:11:48,360 --> 00:11:49,640
Didn't you say before

216
00:11:50,520 --> 00:11:53,050
that you stayed here because you like Nan'an?

217
00:11:53,160 --> 00:11:56,160
You don't have to keep working as a receptionist at my sister's shop.

218
00:11:56,160 --> 00:11:58,560
Doing this, photography, travel shoots,

219
00:11:58,720 --> 00:12:00,520
doesn't it make much more money?

220
00:12:00,840 --> 00:12:02,040
It's a part-time job.

221
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:05,160
And the two don't conflict.

222
00:12:07,320 --> 00:12:08,600
They don't conflict?

223
00:12:09,200 --> 00:12:09,760
No.

224
00:12:10,480 --> 00:12:11,240
No.

225
00:12:11,880 --> 00:12:13,400
They don't conflict.

226
00:12:14,960 --> 00:12:16,880
If they don't conflict,

227
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:19,560
why are you stuttering

228
00:12:20,800 --> 00:12:22,200
and avoiding my eyes?

229
00:12:25,720 --> 00:12:26,720
Feeling guilty?

230
00:12:28,640 --> 00:12:29,360
Damn it.

231
00:12:29,800 --> 00:12:31,080
Did she find out?

232
00:12:31,760 --> 00:12:34,000
Stay calm. Don't panic.

233
00:12:34,720 --> 00:12:37,580
Don't you know men and women shouldn't be too close?

234
00:12:38,960 --> 00:12:39,800
Miss Li.

235
00:12:40,440 --> 00:12:42,000
Getting so close to me,

236
00:12:42,440 --> 00:12:44,040
could it be

237
00:12:44,600 --> 00:12:47,120
that you covet my beauty?

238
00:12:49,560 --> 00:12:50,760
Beauties.

239
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:53,810
Where are the beauties?

240
00:12:54,200 --> 00:12:55,360
Where are they?

241
00:12:55,640 --> 00:12:56,960
Instead of daydreaming,

242
00:12:56,960 --> 00:12:58,400
you should think about

243
00:12:58,600 --> 00:13:01,260
how to get more customers for the travel agency.

244
00:13:07,920 --> 00:13:09,040
That scared me.

245
00:13:09,640 --> 00:13:12,040
If she finds out I'm Golden Spiral,

246
00:13:12,600 --> 00:13:14,200
I'm dead meat.

247
00:13:18,240 --> 00:13:19,480
Wait for me.

248
00:13:19,480 --> 00:13:21,920
I'd be waiting until dark.

249
00:13:36,800 --> 00:13:38,000
Here are your Honglai chicken feet.

250
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:39,720
Eat them while they're hot. They won't taste as good cold.

251
00:13:39,720 --> 00:13:40,720
Okay, okay.

252
00:13:40,720 --> 00:13:41,480
Thank you, thank you.

253
00:13:41,480 --> 00:13:43,080
Can I take a picture with you?

254
00:13:44,960 --> 00:13:46,640
Well-proportioned muscles,

255
00:13:46,640 --> 00:13:47,720
a friendly smile,

256
00:13:47,720 --> 00:13:49,050
and reasonable prices.

257
00:13:49,640 --> 00:13:51,570
This is a good marketing strategy.

258
00:13:52,120 --> 00:13:54,560
Is he selling chicken feet or muscles?

259
00:13:54,760 --> 00:13:57,020
The food industry is so competitive now.

260
00:13:58,440 --> 00:14:00,440
It's called visual marketing.

261
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:02,960
Our travel agency can do the same.

262
00:14:03,040 --> 00:14:04,900
We can find a good-looking guide.

263
00:14:05,360 --> 00:14:07,000
Do I not look good?

264
00:14:08,440 --> 00:14:09,680
Alright, alright.

265
00:14:10,160 --> 00:14:11,400
You are the

266
00:14:13,600 --> 00:14:14,800
refreshing type.

267
00:14:15,200 --> 00:14:16,200
You're different.

268
00:14:16,200 --> 00:14:17,720
I work out too.

269
00:14:18,840 --> 00:14:20,400
It's just that my muscles

270
00:14:20,680 --> 00:14:22,120
are more reserved.

271
00:14:24,280 --> 00:14:25,240
Let's go.

272
00:14:25,240 --> 00:14:27,200
Places that use muscles to attract customers

273
00:14:27,200 --> 00:14:28,760
definitely don't have good food.

274
00:14:28,760 --> 00:14:29,640
If you're not eating, I will.

275
00:14:29,640 --> 00:14:30,770
Marketing can't...

276
00:14:36,240 --> 00:14:39,280
Boss, I want a super large portion of chicken feet.

277
00:14:39,280 --> 00:14:40,080
Okay.

278
00:14:44,240 --> 00:14:45,600
You two are tourists, right?

279
00:14:45,600 --> 00:14:47,120
Honglai chicken feet are a specialty of our Nan'an.

280
00:14:47,120 --> 00:14:48,240
They taste very good.

281
00:14:48,240 --> 00:14:48,880
I know.

282
00:14:49,040 --> 00:14:51,200
Um, boss, I want to ask you something.

283
00:14:51,400 --> 00:14:54,120
Are there more tourists

284
00:14:54,120 --> 00:14:56,250
or locals among your usual customers?

285
00:14:57,640 --> 00:14:59,320
Boss, can you hurry up?

286
00:14:59,320 --> 00:15:00,600
We are in a hurry.

287
00:15:01,520 --> 00:15:02,720
Okay.

288
00:15:03,200 --> 00:15:03,960
Okay.

289
00:15:04,280 --> 00:15:05,480
It will be ready soon.

290
00:15:08,840 --> 00:15:10,000
Your Honglai chicken feet are ready.

291
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:11,260
Welcome to come again.

292
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:12,800
Thank you.

293
00:15:12,800 --> 00:15:13,560
We will come often.

294
00:15:13,560 --> 00:15:15,400
I just wanted to ask you, um...

295
00:15:15,400 --> 00:15:16,200
Not necessarily.

296
00:15:16,200 --> 00:15:17,130
We are very busy.

297
00:15:17,960 --> 00:15:18,880
Let's go.

298
00:15:19,360 --> 00:15:20,840
Don't push, line up.

299
00:15:21,480 --> 00:15:21,880
Everyone will get some.

300
00:15:21,880 --> 00:15:22,400
I want some too.

301
00:15:22,400 --> 00:15:22,960
Let's go.

302
00:15:22,960 --> 00:15:24,960
What are you doing? What's the rush?

303
00:15:24,960 --> 00:15:26,560
I was just about to discuss with someone

304
00:15:26,560 --> 00:15:27,840
to see if we should collaborate on some

305
00:15:27,840 --> 00:15:29,320
food tours or something.

306
00:15:30,400 --> 00:15:32,400
Who asked you to keep staring at him?

307
00:15:32,640 --> 00:15:33,440
What?

308
00:15:35,040 --> 00:15:35,880
I mean,

309
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:39,440
